      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 9, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Priya Nandakumar, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Surveillance colonoscopy."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "Procedure: The colonoscope was advanced to the cecum, identified by the appendiceal orifice and ileocecal valve."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "Findings: In the sigmoid colon at 25 cm there was a 6 mm sessile polyp."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "This polyp was removed en bloc with a cold snare and retrieved."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "A second polyp, 3 mm and flat, was seen in the sigmoid colon at 30 cm."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "Cold forceps biopsies were taken from it, and it was left in place."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "The second polyp was not snared because of its size."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "Impression: Two sigmoid polyps: the 6 mm polyp removed with a cold snare; the 3 mm polyp biopsied and left in place."
    }
  ],
